(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607083500-cloud-itonami-photo-7420-coverage" "2607083600-cloud-itonami-personalservice-9609-coverage" "2607083800-cloud-itonami-edsupport-8550-coverage" "2607084000-cloud-itonami-headoffice-7010-coverage" "2607084300-cloud-itonami-residential-8790-coverage" "2607084400-cloud-itonami-cultural-8542-coverage" "2607084600-cloud-itonami-reserve-6411-coverage" "2607084700-kotoba-lang-apn-cloud-itonami-isic-6110" "2607085600-cloud-itonami-proserv-7490-coverage" "2607085700-cloud-itonami-sportsevent-9319-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic- ADR-0001s" "langgraph ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607085800"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 72, :blueprint 13, :spec 545, :total 630}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/distinctive-check-9329 "emergency-egress-obstructed-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept (grep-verified absent -- zero hits for 'egress' as a standalone check across every prior sibling; the fleet's one prior 'egress' reference, facility.facts's own required-EVIDENCE checklist item, is a document-on-file requirement, not a live obstruction-status check), the 57th distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently sportsevent.governor/anti-doping-control-unresolved-violations at 56th), grounded in real assembly-venue fire/life-safety law: NFPA 101 Life Safety Code (Means of Egress) and Germany's Versammlungsstättenverordnung -- acutely relevant to escape rooms specifically, after real-world escape-room fire incidents prompted dedicated fire-code attention to locked/obscured emergency exits"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607085800: `cloud-itonami-isic-9329` (other amusement/recreation n.e.c.) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607071922 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9321`, amusement parks -- structurally closest sibling)\n- ADR-2607085700 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9319`, sports-event officiating/timing)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-9329/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-9329` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nother amusement and recreation activities not elsewhere classified:\narcades, escape rooms, recreational fishing/hunting operations. Like\nevery prior vertical in this fleet, the blueprint text alone is not\nan implementation -- this ADR records the governed-actor build that\npromotes `cloud-itonami-isic-9329` from `:blueprint` to\n`:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry, the fifty-\neighth vertical built outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/\nreal-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-9329`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   recreation-venue operating model (booking/admission intake,\n   jurisdiction safety verification, operation resumption after a\n   safety hold) but had no governed-actor implementation: no Store,\n   no Governor, no rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text names only ONE real-world act (\"resuming\n   operation after a safety-flagged condition\") -- this build needed\n   the single-actuation shape.\n3. This vertical is structurally the closest sibling to\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-9321` (`parksafety`, amusement parks/rides),\n   which already established a \"resume after safety hold\" actuation\n   shape -- but ISIC 9329's own named example activities (arcades,\n   escape rooms, recreational fishing/hunting) have no mechanical\n   ride-inspection regime, so this build needed to re-derive its own\n   domain-appropriate check family rather than clone `parksafety`'s\n   checks verbatim.\n4. Real-world escape-room fire incidents have made emergency-egress\n   obstruction a genuine, load-bearing regulatory concern for this\n   exact venue category -- no dedicated check for this concept\n   existed anywhere in this fleet, and it needed to be verified\n   absent via grep before being claimed as new.\n5. `facility`/9311 already established a real \"occupancy exceeds\n   capacity\" MAXIMUM-ceiling check for sports-facility venues -- this\n   build's own occupancy check needed to honestly characterize its\n   reuse of that exact concept rather than overclaim novelty.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** The blueprint's own README/business-\n   model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE\n   real-world act. Matching `leasing`/`underwriting`/`testlab`/\n   `clinic`/`veterinary`/`funeral`/`parksafety`/`salon`/\n   `entertainment`/`facility`/`consulting`/`advertising`/`polling`/\n   `research`/`design`/`sports`/`alliedhealth`/`photo`/\n   `personalservice`/`edsupport`/`cultural`/`proserv`/`sportsevent`'s\n   single-actuation shape, `high-stakes` is the one-member set\n   `#{:actuation/resume-operation}` -- a POSITIVE actuation (committing\n   a real resumption record), matching this fleet's majority shape\n   (`3600`/`6190` are the two NEGATIVE-actuation exceptions).\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `venue`. Four ops:\n   `:venue/intake`, `:venue/verify`, `:egress/screen`,\n   `:actuation/resume-operation` (high-stakes).\n3. **`emergency-egress-obstructed-violations` -- the 57th\n   unconditional-evaluation grounding, a genuinely new concept.**\n   Grep-verified absent as a standalone check (the fleet's one prior\n   \"egress\" reference, `facility.facts`'s own required-EVIDENCE\n   checklist item, is a document-on-file requirement, not a live\n   obstruction-status check). Grounded in NFPA 101 Life Safety Code\n   (Means of Egress) and Germany's Versammlungsstättenverordnung.\n   Gates `:egress/screen` and the actuation.\n4. **`occupancy-exceeds-capacity-violations` -- an honest, LITERAL\n   reuse, not claimed as new.** This exact function (`facility.\n   registry/occupancy-exceeds-capacity?`, ISIC 9311's own FIRST\n   non-temporal MAXIMUM-ceiling instance) is re-applied here to a\n   second, genuinely different venue type -- the 13th instance of\n   that family overall, and the first literal re-application of\n   `facility.registry`'s own specific check since it was established.\n   Gates only the actuation.\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:resumed?` on the\n   `venue` record, never a single `:status` value -- the same\n   discipline `parksafety.governor`'s own `:reopened?` guard (the\n   structurally closest sibling) establishes.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/recreation/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor\n   is safely named `venue` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** -- Phase 3's `:auto` set is\n   `{:venue/intake}` only; the actuation is permanently excluded from\n   every phase's `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** -- this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** -- `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** -- the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Seventy-third implemented actor in this fleet's registry (72\n  implemented immediately before this build).\n- Establishes a genuinely NEW unconditional-evaluation-screening\n  concept (emergency-egress-obstructed), grep-verified absent from\n  every prior sibling before the claim was finalized.\n- Documents an honest, literal reuse of `facility.registry`'s own\n  specific MAXIMUM-ceiling check (occupancy-exceeds-capacity), the\n  13th instance of that family, applied to a second venue type for\n  the first time -- not claimed as new.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/recreation/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 72 → 73, `:blueprint` 13 → 12,\n  `:spec` 545 unchanged (sum 630; see Scope note below on the\n  `:total` figure).\n- Test status: 30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four\n  HARD-hold cases).\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing -- 7 tests / 120 assertions,\n  all green.\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Scope note\n\nThis ADR's `:fleet-maturity-before`/`:fleet-maturity-after` `:total`\nfield (630) reflects the actual observed sum of `:implemented` +\n`:blueprint` + `:spec` in `registry.edn` at build time, rather than\n`docs/cloud-itonami.md`'s \"Total entries: 643\" figure -- the same\nclarification ADR-2607085700 (`sportsevent`/9319) already recorded:\nthat 643 figure tracks a separate, pre-existing, wider ISIC-class/\ngroup count, not per-vertical maturity accounting. Not introduced or\nworsened by this build; not in scope to reconcile here.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| Cloning `parksafety.governor`'s checks verbatim (inspection-not-passed, operators-insufficient) | ISIC 9329's named example activities have no mechanical ride-inspection regime and no per-ride staffing minimum -- the real concerns are assembly-venue fire/life-safety, warranting a re-derived check family |\n| Framing `occupancy-exceeds-capacity?` as a new concept for this venue type | It is the exact same real-world concept and field comparison `facility.registry` already established; honest reuse characterization matches this fleet's precedent-verification discipline |\n| A dual-actuation shape (splitting \"resuming operation\" by hazard type) | The blueprint's own text consistently names only ONE real-world act |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9329/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9329/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9329/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9321/src/parksafety/governor.cljc` (structurally closest sibling)\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9311/src/facility/registry.cljc` (`occupancy-exceeds-capacity?` origin)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"9329\"`)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 73, :blueprint 12, :spec 545, :total 630}"), (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-9329 "tested via :egress/screen directly from the start (not via the actuation op against an unscreened venue), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's, banking's, advertising's, polling's, research's, design's, nursing's, sports's, alliedhealth's, laundry's, holdco's, photo's, personalservice's, edsupport's, headoffice's, residential's, cultural's, reserve's, proserv's and sportsevent's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a forty-fifth consecutive vertical"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-9329 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all"), (:adr/honest-reuse-check-9329 "occupancy-exceeds-capacity-violations is an honest, LITERAL reuse of facility.registry/occupancy-exceeds-capacity? (ISIC 9311's own FIRST non-temporal instance of this fleet's MAXIMUM-ceiling family) -- the 13th instance of that family overall, and the FIRST literal re-application of facility.registry's own specific check to a second venue type (grep-verified: no other sibling had reused this specific function by name since facility established it) -- NOT claimed as a new concept"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 9329 (other amusement/recreation activities n.e.c.) contributes a genuinely new check concept (emergency-egress-obstructed?) despite reusing an existing concept (occupancy-exceeds-capacity?, a literal reuse of facility/9311's own check) for its second distinctive check, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention; :fleet-maturity-before/:total reflects the actual observed sum of the three maturity tiers in registry.edn at build time, not the docs/cloud-itonami.md 'Total entries: 643' figure, which tracks a separate, pre-existing, wider ISIC-class/group count (see ADR-2607085700's own scope note for the same clarification)"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/single-actuation-9329 "this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE real-world act (resuming operation after a safety-flagged condition), so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/resume-operation}); a POSITIVE actuation matching this fleet's majority shape (3600/6190 are the two NEGATIVE-actuation exceptions)"), (:adr/test-status-9329 "30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 120 assertions, all green"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-9329"), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-9329 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"9329\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding"), (:adr/pattern-9329 "sealed RecOps-LLM + independent Recreation Safety Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all seventy-one prior actors; FIFTY-EIGHTH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420, 7420, 9609, 8550, 7010, 8790, 8542, 6411, 7490, 9319) -- structurally closest to 9321 (parksafety, resume-after-safety-hold shape), genuinely distinct domain"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-9329 (other amusement/recreation n.e.c.) deepened to :implemented -- fifty-eighth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))